{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And you shall take for yourselves.</b> We believe the words of the translators [the Targum], for they do not contradict the verse, even though we find ויקחו להם איש שה לבית אבות. They also translated that פרי עץ הדר is the etrog, and in truth there is no tree fruit more beautiful (הדר) than it, and they interpreted it as 'הדר in its tree' by way of asmakhta, as I explained in connection with the verse לעם נכרי. The Sadducees said that from these you make sukkot, and brought proof from the book of Ezra — and these, will they not rouse the heart to see that in the book of Ezra there is neither ערבי נחל nor פרי עץ at all, only leaves of five kinds, and no mention of leaves of hadas and leaves of עץ עבות — a charge against our ancestors. Also the species of hadas, its tree is not tall, and behold they are two kinds, tall and short. And the exiled from the land of Kedar to the land of Edom, if he has eyes, he will know the secret of this commandment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ואלה עורי לב הלא יראו' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. 'הגולה מארץ קדר לארץ אדום' is a cryptic sod reference, left untranslated in meaning per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:06.715707191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}